
I made some minor changes to the Makefile to build under Openwindows
X11 header files instead of the /usr/include/X11 paths.  To make Xloadimage
under Openwindows, just type "make own".  I've included the original
MIT-oriented makefile included with the Xloadimage 2.0 distribution
( Makefile.orig ) in case you have problems.

Perhaps someone with gcc loaded can test builiding this with the gcc
flags as well.  Look in the Makefile for the right incantation.

I also added ".im1, .im8, and .im24" to default image file extensions
since this seems to becoming a standard representing Sun raster files
in OWN and other places around Sun.

Enjoy,

Mike
